{"jurisdiction":"NE","generatedAt":"2026-11-05T05:54:04Z","bills":{"NE-2025-LR467":{"id":"NE-2025-LR467","passed":false,"number":"LR 467","title":"Interim study to examine strategies, policies, and investments that cities, villages, and the State of Nebraska may use to make the state more attractive to young people","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-25","sponsor":{"name":"McKinney","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"11"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-09-03","text":"Notice of hearing for November 06, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Urban Affairs Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR467.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR467.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The resolution would direct a Nebraska committee to study ways cities, villages, and the state can make Nebraska more appealing to young people, including students, young workers, entrepreneurs, and early-career families. The study would look at jobs, pay, housing, education and training, arts and culture, transportation, civic life, and barriers that make young people leave or stay away. The committee would then report its findings and recommendations to lawmakers.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR418":{"id":"NE-2025-LR418","passed":false,"number":"LR 418","title":"Interim study to examine inland port authorities, how inland port authoriti