ember 16, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Health and Human Services Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR481.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR481.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The resolution would direct the Health and Human Services Committee to study the fiscal and operational issues of adding long-term care services and supports to the state Medicaid managed care program. It would also look at what other states have spent and what problems they faced when making similar changes. After the study, the committee would report its findings and recommendations to the Legislature or the Legislative Council.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR404":{"id":"NE-2025-LR404","passed":false,"number":"LR 404","title":"Interim study to examine Nebraska statutes and the processes relating to the developmental disability and the aged and disabled waivers and the tools used to assess developmental disabilities","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-24","sponsor":{"name":"Rountree","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"3"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-07-21","text":"Notice of hearing for September 18, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Health and Human Services Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-24","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-24","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR404.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR404.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"This legislative resolution would direct the Health and Human Services Committee to do an interim study, which is a review done between sessions. The study would look at Nebraska laws and the rules and tools used for developmental disability waivers and aged and disabled waivers. It would also review waiver eligibility limits, assessment tools, section 1634 Medicaid status, and algorithm-based assessments, then report its findings and recommendations.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR383":{"id":"NE-2025-LR383","passed":false,"number":"LR 383","title":"Interim study to examine the issue of maternal depression in Nebraska and potential statutory or administrative changes that may support maternal mental health in the state","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-20","sponsor":{"name":"Spivey","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"13"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-07-21","text":"Notice of hearing for September 16, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Health and Human Services Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegisl